WEBVTT

01:53.100 --> 01:57.410
This was a year filled with earthquakes and extreme weather.

01:57.650 --> 02:01.420
It's been predicted that this winter will be colder than in previous years.

02:01.420 --> 02:05.410
So make sure you don't catch colds.

02:05.410 --> 02:11.110
Also, don't eat too much or do things that'll hurt your body...

02:11.110 --> 02:12.350
Don't get out of line.

02:16.400 --> 02:18.980
Ichiko, run!

02:19.640 --> 02:20.770
Tomorrow?

02:20.770 --> 02:22.110
We've got entrance exams next year.

02:22.540 --> 02:25.860
This will probably be the last time we'll be able to relax during a break.

02:25.860 --> 02:27.860
So that's why we're going to Montaro Land?

02:28.060 --> 02:30.430
Yeah, for the Christmas event.

02:30.430 --> 02:31.870
Ono, come with us!

02:32.230 --> 02:33.700
Let me see...

02:33.700 --> 02:36.200
We'll definitely have fun at that amusement park!

02:36.590 --> 02:41.110
Once we're third years, we probably won't have anymore time to have fun together.

02:42.150 --> 02:43.130
So?

02:43.770 --> 02:45.460
All right, I'll go.

02:45.820 --> 02:48.130
I'm bringing Yumemi and Suzume too.

02:48.130 --> 02:50.710
Okay. Tell Hidaka-san and the others about it.

02:50.710 --> 02:51.470
No problem.

02:52.230 --> 02:54.470
I wonder if I should go.

02:55.440 --> 02:58.510
Takashi, this isn't like you at all.

02:58.510 --> 03:00.770
Hmm? I suppose...

03:00.770 --> 03:05.440
Starting today, I know you guys will come over to my family's shrine to help out...

03:05.440 --> 03:08.390
But you see, there won't be much going on at the shrine during Christmas.

03:11.000 --> 03:13.580
You're lucky that you're so carefree.

03:13.580 --> 03:14.070
Huh?

03:14.420 --> 03:17.140
I'm not going there to kill time.

03:17.140 --> 03:18.950
I just want to take Yumemi there.

03:19.380 --> 03:21.330
Hidaka-san?

03:22.960 --> 03:27.250
She's been staring at the sky every day since that floating island incident.

03:27.830 --> 03:29.880
You mean the floating island incident last year?

03:30.330 --> 03:32.260
Yeah, that one.

03:32.780 --> 03:35.310
There's no doubt I saw it.

03:35.810 --> 03:38.020
But Yumemi is dragging it out.

03:38.210 --> 03:42.490
It was a mirage. At least, that's what the news said.

03:42.490 --> 03:46.920
I know everyone else has accepted that explanation, but we haven't...

03:47.530 --> 03:50.030
Yeah, the situation isn't good now.

03:50.330 --> 03:53.490
We need to bring Yumemi's attention back to Earth,

03:53.490 --> 03:56.680
and tomorrow's event is a great chance to do so.

03:58.100 --> 04:00.820
If you're coming, you have to help me.

04:01.970 --> 04:03.290
Don't give me that!

04:03.290 --> 04:05.720
You've known Yumemi for a long time, haven't you?

04:06.220 --> 04:07.540
But I...

04:07.850 --> 04:10.870
You don't want us to cancel our part-time jobs, do you?

04:12.950 --> 04:14.300
I'm counting on you.

04:16.700 --> 04:22.020
Whenever you talk about Hidaka-san, it's like you're a different person.

04:22.850 --> 04:26.770
Of course! I mean... We're friends!

04:26.780 --> 04:28.680
I can't just leave her alone.

04:44.080 --> 04:45.870
It was shaking...

04:45.870 --> 04:48.330
This place won't collapse, right?

04:48.330 --> 04:51.910
It's been standing for a long time, so I think it'll be okay.

04:51.910 --> 04:53.880
That's why I'm worried.

04:54.140 --> 04:57.630
They say this shrine is built on top of a large rock bed.

04:58.150 --> 05:00.380
That's why I heard it'll be okay.

05:00.380 --> 05:02.040
Did you get that from Takashi?

05:02.040 --> 05:02.510
Yeah.

05:03.030 --> 05:04.310
Weird.

05:04.870 --> 05:06.310
Yumemi! Ichiko!

05:07.030 --> 05:08.770
Help me untie this, please...

05:09.060 --> 05:11.220
Gosh, what are you doing?

05:11.220 --> 05:13.400
You've knotted this all wrong.

05:13.400 --> 05:14.610
Didn't I teach you already?

05:14.870 --> 05:15.900
Like this...

05:24.540 --> 05:26.000
Stay still.

05:26.000 --> 05:27.270
It's tight.

05:27.270 --> 05:29.750
That hallucination again...

05:30.560 --> 05:32.380
It's so boring.

05:32.380 --> 05:35.120
It can't be helped since it's the Christmas season.

05:35.120 --> 05:38.190
It's tough when there are so many gods.

05:38.190 --> 05:42.960
I don't think that's the only reason why people don't come and pray here.

05:42.960 --> 05:46.810
Don't you feel as though the gods here can't do much?

05:47.040 --> 05:49.510
Also, I've only heard weird rumors.

05:49.510 --> 05:50.600
Rumors?

05:50.600 --> 05:54.280
Something like seeing spirits, being attacked by some light, etcetera, etcetera.

05:54.540 --> 05:57.160
I'm scared!

05:57.160 --> 05:59.280
So you're afraid of ghosts.

06:03.700 --> 06:04.620
Yumemi!

06:06.880 --> 06:08.550
You're thinking about it again, aren't you?

06:08.550 --> 06:09.410
No...

06:09.410 --> 06:10.730
Really?

06:14.800 --> 06:19.800
I wonder what the deal is with the floating island and that red guy.

06:20.580 --> 06:22.090
Do you mean Munto?

06:22.090 --> 06:23.810
Oh, his name is Munto?

06:24.070 --> 06:27.550
He exists above our heads.

06:27.550 --> 06:29.310
I want to go there!

06:29.310 --> 06:32.140
You make it sound like you'd be able to see him if you could fly.

06:32.140 --> 06:34.230
How should I describe that place?

06:34.230 --> 06:36.180
It's a different world...

06:36.180 --> 06:39.100
There's a wall that we can't break no matter how hard we try.

06:39.100 --> 06:42.890
It's impossible for us to go, got it?

06:44.810 --> 06:47.110
Yumemi, not again!

06:47.110 --> 06:47.950
I'm sorry...

06:48.440 --> 06:50.820
Um... Excuse me.

06:52.770 --> 06:57.550
I have something to do, so could one of you keep an eye on the fire?

06:57.550 --> 06:58.640
Okay.

06:58.640 --> 07:00.230
I'll be right back.

07:01.540 --> 07:03.020
I'll go.

07:20.710 --> 07:22.910
Lend me your power, Yumemi.

07:23.450 --> 07:25.610
The world is in danger of total devastation.

07:26.230 --> 07:29.800
In order to avert this danger, I need your power!

07:30.670 --> 07:36.090
If you don't lend me your power, both the Heavens and your world will be destroyed.

08:07.960 --> 08:11.500
That's what happened when I connected with Munto's world last time...

08:23.270 --> 08:24.380
Yumemi!

08:29.330 --> 08:30.500
Munto?

08:30.500 --> 08:31.590
Is that you, Munto?

08:32.110 --> 08:33.560
What's wrong?

08:33.560 --> 08:35.310
Why are you here?

08:35.310 --> 08:36.340
Munto,

08:37.170 --> 08:38.380
tell me!

08:40.570 --> 08:41.510
Yumemi!

08:42.990 --> 08:44.490
What are you doing?

08:44.490 --> 08:45.550
Are you all right?

08:45.550 --> 08:46.670
Get a grip of yourself!

08:53.370 --> 08:55.940
Munto, why did you come back?

08:57.280 --> 08:59.040
It isn't over...

09:01.470 --> 09:04.310
This is bad, what should I do?

09:04.310 --> 09:05.840
Yumemi, calm yourself down!

09:06.280 --> 09:09.310
Ichiko-san, what's going on?

09:09.310 --> 09:11.260
Hey! What is this rock?

09:13.070 --> 09:14.270
Rock?

09:14.270 --> 09:16.550
Yumemi! Ichiko!

09:20.950 --> 09:22.820
Can you go home by yourself?

09:22.820 --> 09:24.880
Yeah, I'm fine now.

09:25.410 --> 09:26.530
Sorry.

09:29.180 --> 09:30.840
See you later.

09:37.990 --> 09:41.090
Yumemi, are you still not feeling well?

09:43.520 --> 09:45.870
Sis isn't going to eat?

09:45.870 --> 09:48.090
I'll bring something up for her later.

09:54.650 --> 09:57.140
I'm having that feeling again...

10:06.680 --> 10:07.870
Why?

10:09.920 --> 10:12.370
Why do I feel so sad?

10:12.880 --> 10:14.850
What should I do?

10:15.760 --> 10:16.890
Munto...

10:40.190 --> 10:42.110
Damn that Gass. He shouldn't have...

10:59.230 --> 11:00.520
Gntarl.

11:03.200 --> 11:03.960
Don't tell me...

11:25.230 --> 11:28.360
Our dream was born.

11:28.760 --> 11:32.860
This child is the future for us Heavenly beings.

11:33.030 --> 11:38.240
He's Munto, the fated child who will once again bring both order and the cycle of life back to us.

11:38.410 --> 11:39.540
Father!

11:39.540 --> 11:40.750
Mother!

11:41.010 --> 11:44.940
Munto, Mommy and Daddy are returning to the Akuto.

11:44.940 --> 11:46.650
Don't be sad, Munto.

11:46.650 --> 11:49.390
We'll always be by your side.

11:51.220 --> 11:56.470
Why did the former king use the precious Akuto to give birth to a new king...

11:56.470 --> 12:04.520
...when the Heavens are currently in an Akuto crisis?

12:05.180 --> 12:08.090
You are a cursed child, Munto,

12:08.090 --> 12:13.220
because you carry the blood of your
parents, who predicted the cycle of Akuto.

12:13.220 --> 12:15.840
You swallowed their life.

12:15.840 --> 12:21.730
And now, not only your own land, but the entire Heavens are also in danger because of you.

12:22.590 --> 12:29.370
Munto, we, the United Army, will not obey the Magical Kingdom any longer.

12:33.470 --> 12:34.880
Fool.

12:34.880 --> 12:39.890
What use is it to carve up your own land and purify what's left of the Akuto?

12:40.270 --> 12:43.290
The Heavenly people are destined to perish.

12:43.290 --> 12:45.900
This isn't something you can change on your own.

12:46.980 --> 12:51.650
My predictions can no longer uncover the light of hope for the Heavens.

12:52.610 --> 12:55.380
Munto, the Heavens are already...

12:55.380 --> 12:57.290
Don't give up, Ryuely.

12:57.890 --> 12:59.730
I'll definitely find the light of hope.

13:00.680 --> 13:01.830
Yes...

13:01.830 --> 13:08.130
There's no one else, apart from you, who's able to do that.

13:09.400 --> 13:13.510
If so, then let me become your eyes.

13:20.710 --> 13:21.710
I see.

13:21.710 --> 13:23.010
So these are Munto's...

13:24.870 --> 13:26.140
Yumemi...

13:26.140 --> 13:29.560
Yumemi, Ichiko-chan's on the phone!

13:32.040 --> 13:33.690
Are you feeling better now?

13:34.380 --> 13:35.200
Yeah.

13:36.040 --> 13:39.690
I was really worried because you didn't pick up your cell phone.

13:44.980 --> 13:47.780
Can you make it tomorrow?

13:54.610 --> 13:55.880
Yumemi.

13:55.880 --> 13:56.610
Yes?

13:57.120 --> 13:58.520
I'm sorry.

13:58.520 --> 13:59.550
Why?

14:00.180 --> 14:02.680
Do you still remember when we were small?

14:03.070 --> 14:08.230
I wanted so badly to see the sky you saw, so I kind of forced you...

14:09.640 --> 14:11.640
Where the heck is it?!

14:11.640 --> 14:13.190
Look, over there!

14:14.540 --> 14:15.910
I can't see it!

14:15.910 --> 14:18.220
Why are you the only one who's able to see it?

14:18.220 --> 14:19.870
I want to see it too!

14:19.870 --> 14:22.210
Maybe we can see it if we're closer to it.

14:22.210 --> 14:23.280
Closer?

14:25.330 --> 14:26.700
A high place!

14:26.970 --> 14:28.750
You're right, that place!

14:38.090 --> 14:38.710
Look!

14:46.420 --> 14:49.390
In the end, I still couldn't see it.

14:49.960 --> 14:51.900
I was so angry, and I cried.

14:52.850 --> 14:57.590
From that day onwards, you started to use an umbrella, even on sunny days.

15:05.750 --> 15:11.290
Last summer, I finally saw the sky I so wanted to see.

15:12.090 --> 15:15.250
I saw the same sky with the floating islands as you.

15:16.150 --> 15:18.480
I was so happy that I was about to cry,

15:18.480 --> 15:20.690
even though it disappeared in an instant.

15:20.690 --> 15:26.010
But after seeing it, I started to think that the
world in your eyes is too far away from mine.

15:26.770 --> 15:29.400
It's not a place where we can go.

15:29.400 --> 15:35.580
Moreover, no matter how much you think
about that floating island, you won't be happy!

15:35.580 --> 15:36.590
Ichiko...

15:36.590 --> 15:38.010
Listen to me, Yumemi.

15:38.010 --> 15:42.610
What I'm trying to say is that we're always within your reach!

15:48.120 --> 15:50.380
Do you understand, Yumemi?

15:51.490 --> 15:53.630
Those floating islands are unreachable.

15:53.890 --> 15:58.130
That's why... Stay with us, Yumemi.

15:59.420 --> 16:01.260
Thank you, Ichiko.

16:01.940 --> 16:03.640
But I'm sorry.

16:04.840 --> 16:07.670
I don't even understand it myself.

16:08.870 --> 16:09.640
Yumemi...

16:10.270 --> 16:14.510
Ichiko, what should I do?

16:15.330 --> 16:18.640
Ever since that time, I keep seeing things and hearing voices.

16:19.340 --> 16:22.020
I thought it had already ended.

16:22.550 --> 16:24.510
Why does it keep playing over and over in my mind?

16:26.790 --> 16:29.160
Hey, Ichiko...

16:30.780 --> 16:31.910
Save me...

16:59.040 --> 17:00.800
What's going on? What's wrong, Ichiko?!

17:00.800 --> 17:01.930
Is it a burglar?

17:01.930 --> 17:02.700
Where is he?!

17:02.700 --> 17:04.070
Where did he run?!

17:04.070 --> 17:05.140
Idiot.

17:05.140 --> 17:07.970
Idiot?! Did you just call me an idiot?

17:07.970 --> 17:09.410
Why did you call your father an idiot?

17:09.410 --> 17:11.540
Hey, Ichiko!

17:11.780 --> 17:13.690
What's wrong, Tami-chan?

17:13.690 --> 17:14.750
What happened?!

17:14.750 --> 17:16.360
Is Ii-chan all right?

17:16.360 --> 17:18.830
What happened to Ichiko-chan?

17:18.830 --> 17:20.790
She called me an idiot.

17:20.790 --> 17:22.340
Oh, so it was just an argument...

17:22.340 --> 17:23.410
It wasn't!

17:33.620 --> 17:34.590
Yumemi!

17:34.590 --> 17:36.190
Good morning!

17:36.630 --> 17:37.980
What are you doing?

17:37.980 --> 17:39.120
Hurry up!

17:39.120 --> 17:41.190
Montaro is waiting for you!

17:41.690 --> 17:43.440
Come on, hurry up!

17:43.440 --> 17:45.140
Hurry up!

17:45.140 --> 17:47.240
Yumemi, come down!

17:47.470 --> 17:48.470
Yumemi!

17:51.140 --> 17:59.630
<i>Mon-Mon-Montaro and us will still be friends on the other side of space...</i>

17:54.880 --> 17:56.620
Hey, we're over here!

17:59.630 --> 18:03.590
<i>He has the smiling power, so he'll never lose!</i>

18:03.590 --> 18:07.650
<i>Let's go, Ultra Jump!</i>

18:09.470 --> 18:12.220
I came here with Kazuya last month, nyaa!

18:12.430 --> 18:15.100
"Nyaa"... Seriously...

18:15.100 --> 18:16.860
It's Montaro!

18:16.860 --> 18:18.890
Hey, I'm back!

18:22.250 --> 18:26.040
Imamura-san sure knows her way around here.

18:26.040 --> 18:31.540
I can't believe Kazuya-kun actually made it into college with her always annoying him.

18:32.070 --> 18:34.330
You're talking about Takamori-senpai, right?

18:34.330 --> 18:39.520
Although his conduct was terrible, his grades were excellent this year,

18:39.520 --> 18:41.370
so it's only natural for him to make it into college.

18:41.370 --> 18:42.790
He's the total opposite of you.

18:42.790 --> 18:48.930
He's the only child of a rich family, he's handsome, he's strong and he's smart.

18:49.400 --> 18:52.500
Hey, help me take a picture!

18:52.500 --> 18:54.360
But his girlfriend is Suzume-chan...

18:54.360 --> 18:56.210
What's wrong with that?!

18:56.210 --> 18:59.900
All right, I'll take it for you!

18:59.900 --> 19:01.590
Let's get in the picture too.

19:04.050 --> 19:06.250
Takashi, we want to be in it too!

19:06.250 --> 19:07.520
Oh, got it.

19:08.140 --> 19:09.520
How's this?

19:10.210 --> 19:11.600
Not bad.

19:11.600 --> 19:13.490
You all look beautiful!

19:13.490 --> 19:15.100
I'm going to take it now.

19:15.100 --> 19:16.450
Say cheese!

19:22.970 --> 19:25.010
Um... Ichiko-san.

19:25.010 --> 19:25.830
What?

19:25.830 --> 19:29.470
Actually, it's about the big rock you were worried about yesterday.

19:30.090 --> 19:35.430
I was interested in it too, so I looked in some old
books at home, and then I remembered something.

19:35.430 --> 19:40.950
My grandfather told me that rock fell from the sky a long, long time ago.

19:40.950 --> 19:44.190
Is this related to the floating island that Hidaka-san-

19:44.190 --> 19:45.640
All right, stop.

19:45.640 --> 19:46.270
Huh?

19:46.270 --> 19:50.320
Is there any credibility to that story at all?

19:50.320 --> 19:51.340
Well...

19:51.340 --> 19:53.320
Don't go saying anything about it to Yumemi.

19:53.940 --> 19:55.400
Okay...

19:55.400 --> 19:57.590
Thank you, mister!

19:58.590 --> 19:59.990
Yay!

20:00.930 --> 20:04.230
Mon-Mon-Montaro and us wi-

20:05.450 --> 20:06.420
Suzume!

20:06.630 --> 20:08.760
What are you doing?

20:08.760 --> 20:09.860
Are you all right?

20:11.090 --> 20:15.300
Montaro is flying to that place...

20:16.260 --> 20:19.310
I'll get you a new one.

20:19.310 --> 20:21.350
You're so clumsy, Suzume.

20:21.350 --> 20:23.100
You need to get it together.

20:32.150 --> 20:35.820
Did you make this all by yourself?!

20:36.190 --> 20:37.880
I can be useful when I need to be.

20:37.880 --> 20:39.260
It looks yummy!

20:39.260 --> 20:43.320
Since we're all eating together, I made a lot.

20:43.320 --> 20:47.600
I'm kind of surprised that you actually know how to cook!

20:47.600 --> 20:48.910
But I need to have a taste before-

20:48.910 --> 20:50.370
None for you.

20:50.370 --> 20:51.840
Come on, eat up.

20:51.840 --> 20:54.340
I'm going to eat!

20:54.340 --> 20:55.930
Ono, give me some!

20:55.930 --> 20:56.890
Oh, me too!

20:56.890 --> 20:58.850
Only if Suzume can't finish it all.

20:59.990 --> 21:01.080
It's good...

21:01.080 --> 21:02.290
Eat more.

21:04.100 --> 21:07.690
Ichiko, thank you for everything you've done.

21:12.400 --> 21:17.890
So, Takashi-kun, do you want to sample my lunch too?

21:17.890 --> 21:20.310
What's with that tone?

21:21.110 --> 21:21.830
Hidaka-san?

21:26.130 --> 21:27.150
Yumemi?

21:28.390 --> 21:29.000
Yumemi!

21:29.470 --> 21:32.130
Oh, there goes Hidaka-chan again.

21:32.130 --> 21:35.510
It must be hard for Ono; I mean, she has to take care of Imamura <i>and Hidaka.</i>

21:36.530 --> 21:37.760
What is this...?

21:41.660 --> 21:43.560
Yumemi, get a grip on yourself!

21:43.560 --> 21:44.680
There's nothing!

21:44.680 --> 21:46.270
There's nothing over there!

21:48.360 --> 21:51.440
Ichiko, I have to go.

21:52.650 --> 21:54.280
No, I won't let you!

21:55.070 --> 21:56.880
I have to go...

21:56.880 --> 21:59.070
I can't run away.

21:59.430 --> 22:01.770
What's wrong with running away?!

22:01.770 --> 22:03.450
Running away is okay!

22:03.450 --> 22:06.050
No one will blame you!

22:08.490 --> 22:10.840
You can't! You have to stay here!

22:12.110 --> 22:15.900
Ichiko, let her go.

22:17.100 --> 22:18.720
What are you saying, Suzume?!

22:18.720 --> 22:19.970
Yumemi is our-

22:20.380 --> 22:23.220
Ichiko, let's run again!

22:23.580 --> 22:26.980
Like we used to do when we were small, Yumemi, you and I.

22:31.270 --> 22:32.430
What's going on?

22:32.430 --> 22:33.690
Hidaka-san, are you okay?

22:35.350 --> 22:35.820
Yumemi?

22:37.520 --> 22:38.950
What's going on?

22:47.650 --> 22:49.670
Is this an earthquake?

22:55.620 --> 22:56.420
Munto...

24:31.430 --> 24:33.920
So that's the red haired guy Yumemi has been talking about?

24:33.920 --> 24:34.730
Yeah.

24:34.900 --> 24:36.520
It's embarrassingly red, isn't it?

24:36.940 --> 24:39.950
Is that what they call a mistake made in one's youth?

24:39.950 --> 24:43.280
Ichiko, doesn't that mean comets will become bad kids?

24:44.230 --> 24:47.690
Next episode of The World Reflected in the Eyes of a Girl who Looks Up at the Sky:

24:47.690 --> 24:48.900
Trust.
